      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: I wanna get back on this?\nSince why are avatar scanned on runtime instead of a json in the api that says how much performance this avatar takes?\nSince avatars are currently calculated at runtime when the person switches to that avatar. It will mean that even if I don't have that person shown it will calculate that avatar. This means you can crash from a avatar crasher on calculating avatar stats (And yes this does happen).\nIt also take a lagg spike away when someone loads in. (without them shown)\nI only wanna download that avatar stats if I can see that avatar. \nThis will fix performance & safety on the platform.\nI made a post about this some time ago but didn't got any attention\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/vrchat-crashes-from-crasher-avatars-without-them-shown.\nPlease consider no runtime calculation of stats this should be a api thing.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
